# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit study data, results or media. This pipeline reads eye-tracking
# recordings, stimulus videos and saliency maps, and writes score files; none
# of that belongs in a repository. Putting data into git history is effectively
# permanent, so this file is a safety net: keep the repository folder for code.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# raw and resampled gaze data, results
gazedata/
Resample_Output*/
Resample_Output_fps*/
nss_Output*/
auc_Output*/
saliency_frames*/
output*/
results/
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# stimulus videos and generated media
video/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif

# model weights (downloaded automatically on the first run)
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTIONS - these ARE part of the package.
#
# The four landmark/detector models are small (12 MB total) and are bundled so
# a fresh clone runs with no download step, and so the repository works on a
# machine where pip and external downloads are blocked. Same for _vendor\,
# which holds mediapipe unpacked (see the README).
#
# Note that a negated path cannot re-include a file if a parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded, so the directories below have to be un-ignored by name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!models/
!models/**
!_vendor/
!_vendor/**

# local scratch, not part of the package
_face_hand_trial/
trashbin/
_acl_recovery/
_tmp/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# local notes that are not part of the package
DATA_ACCESS.md
